# demand_diff_input_1 -- oracle input batches: the demand-blind pt stream (adds
# + net-removals mirroring the driver's d1/d2 edge retracts). The oracle
# evaluates the plain undemanded program and NETS the pt retractions to the
# surviving rows; the demand retracts (rd1/rd1b) are a query-surface call,
# absent here. ans/getpt = the NET single-hop of pt.
#
# e1: pt adds.
batch
+ pt 1 10
+ pt 1 20
+ pt 3 30
end
# d1: edge-retract of (1,10) (driver retract_edges_silent, after demand-death).
batch
- pt 1 10
end
# d2: edge-retract of (1,20) for the dead key (driver retract_edges_silent).
batch
- pt 1 20
end
